{
  "description": "GET /sessions/listing (docs/session-list-scale-design.md §3.2): one workspace's session list as top-level entries with its folder rows. The server's pg spec (src/apiserver/src/sessions/session-listing.pg.spec.ts) seeds each case and reads it through the route, page by page; the web's Vitest spec (src/web/src/lib/sessionListingFixture.test.ts) feeds the same sessions through sessionProjectListing / sessionFolderListing. Both must give exactly `expected`.",
  "rule": [
    "Scope: the owner's sessions in this workspace in the read's view (open: not completed, not trashed; completed: completed, not trashed), conversations only, no scheduled runs.",
    "A session whose membership names a project is held by that project's entry when the project's coordinator runs in this workspace, or the project has no coordinator. A held session is no entry of its own. A member whose coordinator runs in another workspace is a session entry.",
    "The coordinator is the project's coordinator session in either lifecycle (never one in Trash), wherever it runs.",
    "A project entry is filed in its coordinator's folder; a session in its own. A folder that is not a live folder of this workspace counts as no folder.",
    "Without folderId: the entries in no live folder. With folderId: the entries filed in that folder, and no folder rows.",
    "Order: in the Open view, entries go by the section the web's sessionTimeSections (attention on) draws them in: Pinned (a project entry is pinned when its coordinator is), then Needs you, then Working, then the rest. A session's section is its list row's (`rows`), by src/web/src/lib/sessionGrouping.ts sessionNeedsOwner and sessionIsWorking; a project entry is in Needs you when a member it holds has pendingApprovals, in Working when its `running` is set. Within a section, as the web's compareListed sorts it: placement (listedAt, else createdAt) descending; then createdAt descending; then id ascending.",
    "The Completed view has no Pinned, and its order switches on whether any session of the view in this workspace (every folder counted) is held by a project: none held, GET /sessions?view=completed's order — COALESCE(completedAt, archivedAt) descending, then createdAt descending, then id ascending; any held, placement (listedAt, else createdAt) descending; at the same placement a session before a project (the order sessionProjectListing leaves); then createdAt descending; then id ascending. A cursor written under one order and read under the other starts again from the first page.",
    "A project entry's placedAt is the greatest listedAt (else createdAt) of the members it holds; its spokeAt the greatest lastTurnAt (else createdAt); memberCount how many members it holds here; its createdAt (for order) its coordinator's, else that of the member that placed it; running / jobs whether any member it holds runs / has a background job moving, by workspaceSessionCounts' predicates.",
    "Folder rows (first page, no folderId): every live folder in Open, only those holding a session of the view in Completed, by name (case-insensitive, digits by value), the id settling a tie. rowCount: the rows the folder's page lists (a project is one row). needsYou: how many of its sessions (held members filed with their project) need you; running / jobs: whether any of them runs / has a background job moving — workspaceSessionCounts' predicates.",
    "Paging: each page's `next` is the sort key of its last entry; the next page lists the entries strictly after it, so no entry is skipped or repeated however many share a place."
  ],
  "sessionFields": {
    "id": "the session's name in the case; the server spec gives each case's sessions ids that sort as these names do",
    "workspace": "'here' (default) or 'elsewhere'",
    "lifecycle": "'open' (default) or 'completed'",
    "folder": "a folder of `folders` (this workspace) or of `foreignFolders` (the other workspace), or absent",
    "project": "the project its membership names, or absent",
    "role": "COORDINATOR (the project's coordinator) or TASK (a run of one of its tasks, the default when `project` is set)",
    "activity": "what workspaceSessionCounts counts it as: needsYou (a pending approval on a turn in flight), running or jobs; absent for none. `rows` says what an Open session's list row carries for each",
    "createdAt": "defaults to `defaultCreatedAt`",
    "completedAt": "when a completed session was completed; defaults to its listedAt",
    "archivedAt": "set instead of completedAt on a legacy archived-only row"
  },
  "rows": {
    "description": "What an Open session's list row (GET /sessions, and the listing's own rows) carries for each `activity`: the fields sessionNeedsOwner and sessionIsWorking read. The pg spec asserts the rows the route answers agree; the web spec builds its rows from them.",
    "none": { "status": "AWAITING_INPUT", "phase": "IDLE", "released": false, "pendingApprovals": 0 },
    "needsYou": { "status": "RUNNING", "phase": "RUNNING", "released": false, "pendingApprovals": 1 },
    "running": { "status": "RUNNING", "phase": "RUNNING", "released": false, "pendingApprovals": 0 },
    "jobs": { "status": "AWAITING_INPUT", "phase": "RUNNING", "released": false, "pendingApprovals": 0 }
  },
  "defaultCreatedAt": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
